Hello admin,

I am attempting to create a PCA plot using a SNP dataset obtained from the Dartseq method. I have filtered the SNPs using the dart package function. However, when I attempt to generate the PCA plot using the following command, an error occurs. Could you please assist me in identifying what is wrong with the command line? It appears that there may be an issue with the genlight data (f4).

Thank you.

> library(dartR) > library(directlabels) > library(plotly) > pcoa <- gl.pcoa(f4) Starting gl.pcoa   Processing genlight object with SNP data  Performing a PCA, individuals as entities, loci as attributes, SNP genotype as state Completed: gl.pcoa  > gl.pcoa.plot(glPca = pcoa, +  x= f4, +  interactive = TRUE) Starting gl.pcoa.plot   Processing an ordination file (glPca)  Processing genlight object with SNP data Error in data.frame(..., check.names = FALSE) : arguments imply differing number of rows: 45, 0

